<title>UK: Harrisons &amp; Crosfield sells palm oil stake.</title>
<headline>Harrisons &amp; Crosfield sells palm oil stake.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK chemicals to building supplies and animal feeds group Harrisons and Crosfield Plc said on Friday it had sold its 54 percent stake in New Britain Palm Oil Ltd to the state of Papua New Guinea.</p>
<p>The sale, which was completed today, raised $65.5 million, the group said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
